NODE id=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/server.Server.handleStream kind=method
  digest=b3:9d96fe0d21a14cc7b9eb0106f7d086864f5430a82ae1866b84194ea1811c47d1 file=layerx/internal/server/server.go range=807:883 lang=go exported=false byte_range=29645:32169
  sig=func (s *Server) handleStream(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
  doc=handleStream is the PUBLIC live event stream (SSE) backing the explorer — the\nscalable replacement for polling /v1/transfers. It emits `transfer` events\n(id = seq) as payments are accepted and `anchor` events as batches settle. On\n(re)connect it replays any transfers missed since the client's Last-Event-ID\nfrom the DB before joining the live tail, so no payment is ever silently\ndropped; a client that falls too far behind is told to resync + reconnect.
EDGES
  ^contains=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/server.Server
  ^defines=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/server/server.go

